// Java's string literal. Same shape as lib/dq-strings.abnf, but decoded by
// jUnescape, which knows Java's octal escapes ("A\102") and \s.
// The escape set is Java's own (JLS 3.10.7), not lib/dq-strings' "backslash plus
// any printable": `"\!"` is illegal.esc.char, and StrEsc accepted it.
